  "description": "COBOT-EX 2026 — Inter-College Hackathon Build. Innovate. Compete. COBOT-EX 2026 is an inter-college hackathon organized by the Crescent Club of Cobotics at B. S. Abdur Rahman Crescent Institute of Science and Technology, Chennai. The hackathon invites college students to develop innovative, technology-driven solutions and demonstrate their creativity, technical abilities, and problem-solving skills. Event Details Date: 10 November 2026 Venue: B. S. Abdur Rahman Crescent Institute of Science and Technology, Vandalur, Chennai, Tamil Nadu Registration deadline: 5 November 2026 Registration fee: ₹250 per team Prize pool: ₹5,000 Team size: 1–2 members Eligibility Open to college students from institutions across India. Participants must register within the deadline and follow the official event instructions. Participation Process Register for the COBOT-EX 2026 Hackathon. Provide the required participant and team details. Review the official problem statement, rules, and submission instructions provided by the organizers. Participate on the scheduled event date and submit your solution as instructed. Rules Each team may have 1–2 members. Each team must complete its own registration. Participants must follow the official problem statement, deadlines, and submission requirements. Plagiarism, misrepresentation, or unauthorized use of another team's work is not permitted. Organizers' decisions regarding evaluation and prizes will be final, subject to the published rules. Prizes A total prize pool of ₹5,000 is allocated to the Hackathon. Why Participate? Showcase your technical skills, collaborate with fellow innovators, develop practical solutions, and compete with students from other colleges.",
